WEBVTT

00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:05.952
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.210
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:09.051 --> 00:00:09.687
Mary!

00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:10.481
No!

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:13.452
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:14.684 --> 00:00:16.075
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:18.145 --> 00:00:19.557
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:21.383
I can't do this alone.

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:24.788
No!

00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:28.510
We got work to do.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.613
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:33.825
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:33.963 --> 00:00:35.910
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:37.266
You know, saving people,

00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:38.373
Hunting things,

00:00:38.428 --> 00:00:39.342
Family business.

00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:39.840
No.

00:00:39.951 --> 00:00:41.267
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:41.361 --> 00:00:42.785
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.228
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:00:44.256 --> 00:00:44.662
Right?

00:00:46.468 --> 00:00:47.668
Yeah. I know.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.248
Nervous flyer?

00:01:31.104 --> 00:01:32.397
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:33.507 --> 00:01:35.775
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:36.749
I mean, what

00:01:36.918 --> 00:01:37.949
20,000 to one?

00:01:41.809 --> 00:01:42.334
Wow.

00:01:43.084 --> 00:01:44.996
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:10.872 --> 00:02:11.359
Thanks.

00:02:12.146 --> 00:02:12.615
Miranda,

00:02:12.784 --> 00:02:13.421
How are you today?

00:02:13.605 --> 00:02:14.842
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:16.454 --> 00:02:17.616
Welcome aboard.

00:02:18.328 --> 00:02:21.083
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:25.259
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:28.102 --> 00:02:29.470
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:34.786 --> 00:02:35.442
Um...

00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:38.647
Uh, 11F,

00:02:38.703 --> 00:02:40.615
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:02:42.823 --> 00:02:43.535
...the left.

00:02:55.529 --> 00:02:56.241
Excuse me.

00:02:57.044 --> 00:02:58.319
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:02:58.431 --> 00:03:00.793
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:03:01.823 --> 00:03:02.386
Wow.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.050
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:07.403 --> 00:03:08.115
Excuse me.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.670
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:36.332 --> 00:03:37.661
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:04:49.793 --> 00:04:50.674
Morning, sunshine.

00:04:52.039 --> 00:04:52.807
What time is it?

00:04:52.957 --> 00:04:54.269
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:55.131
In the morning?

00:04:55.206 --> 00:04:55.600
Yep.

00:04:55.806 --> 00:04:56.871
Where does the day go?

00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:00.020
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:00.226 --> 00:05:01.575
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.288
You, liar

00:05:03.256 --> 00:05:04.381
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:05.131 --> 00:05:06.930
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:07.808
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:07.864 --> 00:05:08.745
It's riveting tv.

00:05:09.176 --> 00:05:10.563
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:10.807 --> 00:05:11.388
I don't know,

00:05:11.463 --> 00:05:13.053
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:13.241 --> 00:05:13.971
Yeah, it is.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:15.864
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:15.902 --> 00:05:17.232
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:17.251 --> 00:05:19.781
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:21.198 --> 00:05:22.773
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:28.264 --> 00:05:28.807
Yeah.

00:05:30.585 --> 00:05:32.272
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:32.703 --> 00:05:34.408
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:35.905 --> 00:05:36.805
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:37.123 --> 00:05:39.129
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:40.441 --> 00:05:41.003
So, what?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:41.603
All this it...

00:05:41.915 --> 00:05:42.946
Never keeps you up at night?

00:05:44.108 --> 00:05:44.576
Never?

00:05:44.932 --> 00:05:45.645
You're never afraid?

00:05:45.926 --> 00:05:46.807
No, not really.

00:05:55.129 --> 00:05:55.913
That's not fear.

00:05:57.225 --> 00:05:58.125
That is precaution.

00:05:58.706 --> 00:05:59.605
All right, whatever.

00:05:59.643 --> 00:06:00.749
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:09.703 --> 00:06:10.246
Hello?

00:06:10.525 --> 00:06:10.974
Dean,

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.905
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:13.886 --> 00:06:15.901
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:16.985 --> 00:06:17.937
Oh, all right,

00:06:17.981 --> 00:06:20.771
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:22.143
It's not back, is it?

00:06:22.342 --> 00:06:22.807
No.

00:06:23.184 --> 00:06:23.715
No.

00:06:24.955 --> 00:06:25.774
Thank god, no.

00:06:27.254 --> 00:06:29.003
But it's something else, and...

00:06:29.512 --> 00:06:30.862
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.058
What is it?

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:33.648
Can we talk in person?

00:06:39.427 --> 00:06:41.176
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:41.281 --> 00:06:43.823
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:06:44.775 --> 00:06:46.280
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:06:46.878 --> 00:06:48.516
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:06:48.583 --> 00:06:49.225
Poltergeist?

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.328
Man, I loved that movie.

00:06:50.372 --> 00:06:52.232
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.907
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:06:56.903 --> 00:06:57.855
Tell you something

00:06:58.493 --> 00:06:59.799
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.061
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:03.261 --> 00:07:05.033
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:05.652 --> 00:07:06.870
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:07.158 --> 00:07:08.287
Taking some time off.

00:07:08.575 --> 00:07:10.169
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:10.612 --> 00:07:11.962
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:13.331 --> 00:07:13.951
He did?

00:07:14.327 --> 00:07:15.323
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.781
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:19.309
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.434
He's, um

00:07:22.023 --> 00:07:23.352
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:23.617 --> 00:07:25.145
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.363
We get sam.

00:07:26.518 --> 00:07:27.691
Even trade, huh?

00:07:28.223 --> 00:07:29.684
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:30.304 --> 00:07:31.964
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:33.823 --> 00:07:34.930
I listened to this.

00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:35.926
Well,

00:07:36.169 --> 00:07:37.653
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:37.919 --> 00:07:39.889
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.737
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:07:44.025 --> 00:07:44.933
It was one of ours.

00:07:45.456 --> 00:07:45.905
Mayday

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.221
Took off from here,

00:08:09.783 --> 00:08:11.555
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:13.945
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:14.147 --> 00:08:16.490
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:16.848 --> 00:08:18.145
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.083
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:21.056 --> 00:08:21.837
Pilot was one.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.380
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:24.962 --> 00:08:25.929
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:27.589 --> 00:08:28.887
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:30.581
Like it was his fault.

00:08:31.416 --> 00:08:32.223
You don't think it was?

00:08:32.766 --> 00:08:33.614
No, I don't.

00:08:34.334 --> 00:08:34.810
Jerry,

00:08:34.996 --> 00:08:36.836
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:36.921 --> 00:08:38.390
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:38.907
All right.

00:08:39.026 --> 00:08:39.661
And huh...

00:08:39.741 --> 00:08:41.277
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:41.958 --> 00:08:43.190
The other stuff is no problem,

00:08:43.243 --> 00:08:44.064
But the wreckage

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.803
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:08:48.782 --> 00:08:50.292
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:08:52.858 --> 00:08:53.348
No problem.

00:08:58.786 --> 00:08:59.237
Hey

00:08:59.395 --> 00:08:59.859
Hi.

00:09:02.825 --> 00:09:03.831
You've been in there forever.

00:09:05.358 --> 00:09:06.391
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:07.132 --> 00:09:08.245
Homeland security?

00:09:09.423 --> 00:09:10.337
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.118
Even for us.

00:09:11.953 --> 00:09:12.456
Yeah, well,

00:09:12.495 --> 00:09:13.820
It's something new, you know?

00:09:13.833 --> 00:09:15.528
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:20.337 --> 00:09:21.260
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:21.479 --> 00:09:22.121
Well,

00:09:22.136 --> 00:09:24.702
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:24.812 --> 00:09:25.156
Yeah?

00:09:25.234 --> 00:09:25.735
Listen.

00:09:33.412 --> 00:09:34.429
"No survivors"?

00:09:35.321 --> 00:09:36.051
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:36.061 --> 00:09:37.532
There were seven survivors.

00:09:38.122 --> 00:09:38.748
Got me.

00:09:40.996 --> 00:09:42.514
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:44.587
There's a long history of spirits and

00:09:44.634 --> 00:09:46.638
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:09:46.685 --> 00:09:47.749
Like phantom travelers.

00:09:47.796 --> 00:09:48.203
Mm-Hmm

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.160
Or remember flight 401?

00:09:50.394 --> 00:09:50.848
Right

00:09:51.068 --> 00:09:51.835
The one that crashed,

00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:53.384
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:09:53.447 --> 00:09:54.527
Put it in other planes,

00:09:54.836 --> 00:09:57.074
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:09:57.137 --> 00:09:57.481
Right.

00:09:57.544 --> 00:09:58.029
Yep.

00:09:58.984 --> 00:10:00.205
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:10:00.941 --> 00:10:03.320
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:03.373 --> 00:10:05.094
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:05.188 --> 00:10:05.767
Why him?

00:10:05.814 --> 00:10:07.020
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:07.072 --> 00:10:07.823
And two,

00:10:08.402 --> 00:10:09.780
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:10.421 --> 00:10:10.954
He did.

00:10:12.112 --> 00:10:12.973
What makes you say that?

00:10:13.317 --> 00:10:14.554
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:15.359 --> 00:10:16.706
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:19.447 --> 00:10:20.370
I don't understand.

00:10:20.382 --> 00:10:22.329
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:22.681 --> 00:10:23.270
Right.

00:10:23.776 --> 00:10:25.308
Some new information has come up.

00:10:25.544 --> 00:10:27.464
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:29.016
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:29.707 --> 00:10:32.031
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:32.368 --> 00:10:33.092
Like what?

00:10:33.884 --> 00:10:35.113
Strange lights,

00:10:35.787 --> 00:10:37.101
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.208
Voices.

00:10:40.128 --> 00:10:40.936
No, nothing.

00:10:42.869 --> 00:10:43.711
Mr. Joffey

00:10:44.671 --> 00:10:45.143
Jaffey.

00:10:45.446 --> 00:10:45.951
Jaffey.

00:10:46.086 --> 00:10:47.231
You checked yourself in here,

00:10:47.349 --> 00:10:47.804
Right?

00:10:49.019 --> 00:10:49.815
Can I ask why?

00:10:50.312 --> 00:10:51.619
I was a little stressed.

00:10:51.639 --> 00:10:53.490
I survived a plane crash.

00:10:55.156 --> 00:10:55.733
And that's

00:10:55.833 --> 00:10:56.629
What terrified you?

00:10:56.669 --> 00:10:57.803
That's what you were afraid of?

00:10:57.902 --> 00:11:00.410
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:11:00.589 --> 00:11:02.380
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:03.415 --> 00:11:04.410
We need to know what.

00:11:05.478 --> 00:11:05.956
No.

00:11:06.095 --> 00:11:07.170
No, I was...

00:11:07.309 --> 00:11:08.065
Delusional

00:11:08.844 --> 00:11:09.800
Seeing things.

00:11:11.105 --> 00:11:12.125
He was seeing things.

00:11:15.676 --> 00:11:16.271
It's okay.

00:11:17.737 --> 00:11:20.664
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:25.307 --> 00:11:26.038
There was...

00:11:26.277 --> 00:11:26.849
This...

00:11:27.198 --> 00:11:27.866
Man.

00:11:29.551 --> 00:11:30.441
And, uh,

00:11:30.536 --> 00:11:31.951
He had these...

00:11:33.047 --> 00:11:33.670
Eyes...

00:11:33.765 --> 00:11:34.512
These, uh...

00:11:36.587 --> 00:11:37.795
Black eyes.

00:11:39.607 --> 00:11:41.435
And I saw him

00:11:42.215 --> 00:11:44.377
I thought I saw him...

00:11:48.319 --> 00:11:48.923
What?

00:11:51.214 --> 00:11:53.391
He opened the emergency exit.

00:11:55.586 --> 00:11:56.190
But that's...

00:11:56.238 --> 00:11:57.351
That's impossible,

00:11:57.764 --> 00:11:59.022
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:11:59.054 --> 00:11:59.944
There's something like

00:12:00.103 --> 00:12:02.200
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:04.364 --> 00:12:04.936
Yeah...

00:12:05.842 --> 00:12:06.732
This man, huh...

00:12:06.812 --> 00:12:09.307
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:09.564 --> 00:12:11.948
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:13.733 --> 00:12:15.052
What are you, nuts?

00:12:17.293 --> 00:12:18.437
He was a passenger.

00:12:18.469 --> 00:12:20.376
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:27.485 --> 00:12:28.645
Say here we are

00:12:28.757 --> 00:12:30.902
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:31.538 --> 00:12:32.047
Hmm.

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:35.196
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:37.691 --> 00:12:39.725
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:40.109 --> 00:12:43.097
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:12:44.069 --> 00:12:45.086
Not if you're human.

00:12:46.437 --> 00:12:48.423
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:12:48.754 --> 00:12:50.915
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:12:51.344 --> 00:12:53.124
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:13:01.756 --> 00:13:03.059
This is your late husband?

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.523
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:06.344 --> 00:13:07.441
And you said he was a...

00:13:08.299 --> 00:13:09.094
Dentist?

00:13:09.514 --> 00:13:10.097
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:11.374 --> 00:13:13.683
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:16.547 --> 00:13:18.594
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:22.257 --> 00:13:23.666
For him to go like that...

00:13:26.313 --> 00:13:27.553
How long were you married?

00:13:29.957 --> 00:13:31.159
13 years.

00:13:31.916 --> 00:13:33.118
In all that time,

00:13:34.714 --> 00:13:36.442
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:36.836 --> 00:13:38.339
Strange about him,

00:13:38.864 --> 00:13:40.479
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:13:43.684 --> 00:13:44.379
Well...

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.682
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:13:48.813 --> 00:13:49.883
If that's what you mean.

00:13:54.017 --> 00:13:55.202
I mean it goes without saying.

00:13:55.221 --> 00:13:56.635
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:13:57.037 --> 00:13:58.652
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:00.399
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:14:01.169 --> 00:14:03.310
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:03.328 --> 00:14:04.812
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:06.654 --> 00:14:07.555
Okay.

00:14:07.799 --> 00:14:08.764
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:08.793 --> 00:14:09.638
We'd better look the part.

00:14:16.016 --> 00:14:18.253
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:18.572 --> 00:14:19.398
No, you don't.

00:14:19.886 --> 00:14:21.107
You look more like a...

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.854
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:25.694 --> 00:14:26.896
I hate this thing.

00:14:26.933 --> 00:14:27.365
Hey.

00:14:27.741 --> 00:14:29.450
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:13.444 --> 00:15:14.158
What is that?

00:15:15.322 --> 00:15:16.487
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:16.937 --> 00:15:18.646
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:19.437 --> 00:15:21.291
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:21.309 --> 00:15:23.751
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:24.804 --> 00:15:26.006
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:26.757 --> 00:15:27.714
It's homemade.

00:15:29.818 --> 00:15:31.677
Yeah, I can see that.

00:15:58.219 --> 00:15:59.778
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:05.433 --> 00:16:06.372
What is this stuff?

00:16:06.503 --> 00:16:07.818
One way to find out.

00:16:20.681 --> 00:16:21.864
Homeland security?

00:16:22.697 --> 00:16:23.166
What?

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.706
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:25.345 --> 00:16:26.190
What are you talking about?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.539
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:08.927 --> 00:17:10.918
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:12.439 --> 00:17:13.209
Listen Chuck

00:17:13.378 --> 00:17:14.429
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:14.977 --> 00:17:16.460
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:16.779 --> 00:17:17.606
Not even a horse

00:17:17.756 --> 00:17:18.545
More like a pony.

00:17:19.561 --> 00:17:20.481
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.490
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:23.411 --> 00:17:24.218
Look, Chuck,

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:25.927
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:26.303 --> 00:17:27.110
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:28.032 --> 00:17:28.746
No, the...

00:17:29.854 --> 00:17:30.849
The waiting is worse.

00:17:33.328 --> 00:17:35.169
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:08.365 --> 00:18:08.928
Huh.

00:18:10.599 --> 00:18:12.045
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:12.327 --> 00:18:12.947
You're sure?

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:14.487
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:14.506 --> 00:18:15.876
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:15.876 --> 00:18:17.210
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:17.247 --> 00:18:18.675
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:25.603 --> 00:18:25.998
Hmm.

00:18:26.974 --> 00:18:29.754
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:29.857 --> 00:18:30.833
Demonic possession?

00:18:31.378 --> 00:18:34.495
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:34.666 --> 00:18:36.074
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:36.318 --> 00:18:37.013
It's possible.

00:18:37.316 --> 00:18:39.701
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.602
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:40.659 --> 00:18:42.180
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:18:42.217 --> 00:18:44.152
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:18:44.283 --> 00:18:45.992
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:18:46.182 --> 00:18:46.707
Never.

00:18:52.623 --> 00:18:53.299
I'm ready.

00:18:53.506 --> 00:18:54.332
Let's do this.

00:19:02.588 --> 00:19:03.395
How you feeling?

00:19:03.658 --> 00:19:04.466
I feel great.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.531
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:06.907 --> 00:19:07.752
I hope so.

00:19:11.472 --> 00:19:12.298
How long we been up?

00:19:12.862 --> 00:19:14.608
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:14.965 --> 00:19:15.416
Wow.

00:19:15.773 --> 00:19:16.768
Time really does fly.

00:19:44.049 --> 00:19:44.669
So,

00:19:45.063 --> 00:19:47.166
Every religion in every world culture

00:19:47.223 --> 00:19:50.077
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:19:50.426 --> 00:19:53.374
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:19:53.468 --> 00:19:55.140
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:19:55.234 --> 00:19:56.360
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:19:56.398 --> 00:19:57.806
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:19:57.844 --> 00:20:00.567
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:20:00.612 --> 00:20:01.476
Both natural

00:20:01.589 --> 00:20:02.453
And man-Made

00:20:02.509 --> 00:20:04.762
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:04.781 --> 00:20:06.340
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:10.607 --> 00:20:11.771
All right, so, what?

00:20:11.809 --> 00:20:13.837
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:13.875 --> 00:20:15.602
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:16.522 --> 00:20:17.106
Yeah.

00:20:18.252 --> 00:20:18.853
You know,

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:22.120
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:27.026 --> 00:20:27.533
What?

00:20:29.091 --> 00:20:31.082
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:31.645 --> 00:20:33.298
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:33.373 --> 00:20:35.251
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:36.246 --> 00:20:36.960
This is big.

00:20:38.389 --> 00:20:39.516
I wish dad was here.

00:20:40.587 --> 00:20:41.845
Yeah. Me too.

00:20:48.609 --> 00:20:48.984
Hello?

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:50.167
Dean it's Jerry

00:20:50.355 --> 00:20:51.069
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:20:51.369 --> 00:20:52.327
My pilot friend...

00:20:54.318 --> 00:20:55.444
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:20:57.437 --> 00:20:57.925
Wha...

00:20:58.301 --> 00:20:59.446
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:01.850
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:21:01.925 --> 00:21:02.939
About an hour ago.

00:21:03.578 --> 00:21:04.423
The plane went down.

00:21:04.799 --> 00:21:05.587
Where'd this happen?

00:21:05.907 --> 00:21:08.066
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:08.632 --> 00:21:10.078
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:10.322 --> 00:21:10.885
I'm sorry?

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:11.637
Nothing.

00:21:12.369 --> 00:21:14.303
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:17.258
Another crash?

00:21:17.465 --> 00:21:17.990
Yeah.

00:21:18.366 --> 00:21:18.836
Let's go.

00:21:19.042 --> 00:21:19.587
Where?

00:21:20.282 --> 00:21:20.901
Nazareth.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:33.792
Sulfur?

00:21:36.498 --> 00:21:37.681
Well, that's great.

00:21:38.414 --> 00:21:41.174
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.278
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:21:43.684 --> 00:21:44.773
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:21:45.863 --> 00:21:47.966
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:21:48.379 --> 00:21:49.186
What's the bad news?

00:21:49.374 --> 00:21:51.947
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:21:52.112 --> 00:21:52.995
And get this

00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:54.741
So did flight 2485.

00:21:55.042 --> 00:21:55.849
40 minutes?

00:21:56.262 --> 00:21:56.938
What does that mean?

00:21:57.521 --> 00:21:58.835
It's biblical numerology.

00:21:59.098 --> 00:22:01.089
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:22:01.145 --> 00:22:02.122
The number means death.

00:22:02.518 --> 00:22:03.250
I went back,

00:22:03.325 --> 00:22:05.992
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:08.809
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:09.861 --> 00:22:10.743
Any survivors?

00:22:11.419 --> 00:22:11.889
No.

00:22:12.331 --> 00:22:12.856
Or not

00:22:12.932 --> 00:22:14.002
Until now,at least

00:22:14.021 --> 00:22:16.312
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:17.363 --> 00:22:18.809
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:18.922 --> 00:22:20.180
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:20.481 --> 00:22:21.345
"No survivors."

00:22:25.331 --> 00:22:26.702
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:27.922 --> 00:22:29.012
Something finish the job.

00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:33.427
Really?

00:22:34.046 --> 00:22:35.812
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.145
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:37.164 --> 00:22:40.018
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:40.751 --> 00:22:41.220
Thanks.

00:22:41.671 --> 00:22:42.309
All right.

00:22:42.424 --> 00:22:45.072
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:22:45.186 --> 00:22:46.557
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:22:46.614 --> 00:22:49.149
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:22:49.412 --> 00:22:49.937
Right

00:22:49.975 --> 00:22:52.078
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:22:52.116 --> 00:22:53.675
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:22:53.712 --> 00:22:55.064
That sounds like just our luck.

00:22:55.383 --> 00:22:56.998
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:22:57.129 --> 00:22:58.575
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:22:59.159 --> 00:23:00.724
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:23:00.742 --> 00:23:02.066
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:02.121 --> 00:23:03.482
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:05.587
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:06.630 --> 00:23:08.382
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:08.438 --> 00:23:09.127
We'll make it.

00:23:23.462 --> 00:23:24.096
Right there.

00:23:24.208 --> 00:23:25.326
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:25.475 --> 00:23:26.052
Okay.

00:23:26.593 --> 00:23:27.953
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:28.004 --> 00:23:28.992
We need to find a phone.

00:23:32.175 --> 00:23:33.107
Airport Services.

00:23:33.218 --> 00:23:34.299
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:34.369 --> 00:23:35.524
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:35.636 --> 00:23:37.253
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:37.275 --> 00:23:39.168
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:39.311 --> 00:23:40.588
Flight 424.

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:41.755
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:23:42.019 --> 00:23:43.737
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:23:43.825 --> 00:23:45.630
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:23:48.569 --> 00:23:49.626
Come on.

00:23:51.233 --> 00:23:52.467
This is amanda walker.

00:23:52.841 --> 00:23:53.611
Miss walker.

00:23:54.052 --> 00:23:55.862
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:23:55.884 --> 00:23:58.064
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:23:58.394 --> 00:24:00.222
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:01.125
Why Karen?

00:24:01.169 --> 00:24:03.282
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:03.317 --> 00:24:04.836
But she was injured, so

00:24:04.968 --> 00:24:07.962
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:11.227 --> 00:24:11.844
You what?

00:24:11.932 --> 00:24:12.790
Five minutes ago.

00:24:12.834 --> 00:24:15.499
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:15.521 --> 00:24:16.467
Who is this?

00:24:17.668 --> 00:24:18.681
Uh, well...

00:24:19.099 --> 00:24:20.200
There must be some mistake.

00:24:20.222 --> 00:24:22.248
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:23.987 --> 00:24:25.594
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:27.243 --> 00:24:28.322
Guilty as charged.

00:24:29.136 --> 00:24:31.206
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:32.065 --> 00:24:33.694
He's really sorry.

00:24:34.333 --> 00:24:35.918
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:35.962 --> 00:24:37.723
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:37.811 --> 00:24:38.733
Yes, but...

00:24:39.085 --> 00:24:40.758
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:41.089 --> 00:24:41.815
So

00:24:41.925 --> 00:24:43.401
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:24:43.599 --> 00:24:44.634
Don't be like that.

00:24:45.098 --> 00:24:46.199
Come on. The guy's

00:24:46.354 --> 00:24:47.983
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:24:49.326 --> 00:24:50.009
Really?

00:24:50.229 --> 00:24:50.977
Oh, yeah.

00:24:51.638 --> 00:24:53.157
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:24:53.168 --> 00:24:55.260
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:24:55.414 --> 00:24:57.176
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:03.892 --> 00:25:04.817
How are you?

00:25:06.226 --> 00:25:07.393
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:15.370 --> 00:25:16.272
Damn it!

00:25:16.779 --> 00:25:17.858
So close.

00:25:20.368 --> 00:25:22.063
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:22.537 --> 00:25:23.594
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:23.704 --> 00:25:25.377
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:25.476 --> 00:25:26.092
Dean,

00:25:26.225 --> 00:25:27.392
That plane is leaving

00:25:27.436 --> 00:25:28.955
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:28.977 --> 00:25:29.902
And if we're right,

00:25:30.541 --> 00:25:31.840
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:31.994 --> 00:25:32.632
I know.

00:25:32.743 --> 00:25:33.315
Okay.

00:25:33.408 --> 00:25:36.094
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:36.138 --> 00:25:38.274
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:38.318 --> 00:25:39.507
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:39.573 --> 00:25:40.872
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:25:42.876 --> 00:25:43.889
Are you okay?

00:25:46.256 --> 00:25:47.533
No, not really.

00:25:48.810 --> 00:25:49.955
What? What's wrong?

00:25:52.124 --> 00:25:54.150
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:25:56.285 --> 00:25:57.100
Flying?

00:25:57.519 --> 00:25:59.236
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:25:59.578 --> 00:26:00.436
You're joking, right?

00:26:00.502 --> 00:26:01.647
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:03.431 --> 00:26:05.016
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:06.139 --> 00:26:07.923
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:08.212 --> 00:26:08.608
What?

00:26:08.630 --> 00:26:09.665
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:10.216 --> 00:26:11.008
Are you, nuts?

00:26:11.559 --> 00:26:12.924
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:12.968 --> 00:26:14.972
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:15.016 --> 00:26:16.887
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:17.658 --> 00:26:18.583
Come on!

00:26:20.279 --> 00:26:20.962
Really?

00:26:23.274 --> 00:26:24.132
Man...

00:26:37.056 --> 00:26:39.015
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:08.878 --> 00:27:09.847
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:09.869 --> 00:27:11.014
Calms me down.

00:27:13.172 --> 00:27:14.031
Look, man,

00:27:14.405 --> 00:27:15.528
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:15.550 --> 00:27:17.113
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:18.452 --> 00:27:18.959
Okay.

00:27:18.981 --> 00:27:19.883
I mean, we got

00:27:19.994 --> 00:27:22.834
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:22.878 --> 00:27:26.159
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:26.181 --> 00:27:28.360
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:28.449 --> 00:27:30.078
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:31.792 --> 00:27:32.540
Now,

00:27:32.662 --> 00:27:34.687
Who is it possessing?

00:27:35.766 --> 00:27:37.020
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:37.021 --> 00:27:38.078
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:38.100 --> 00:27:40.214
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:40.621 --> 00:27:43.395
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:27:45.476 --> 00:27:46.071
Well,

00:27:46.269 --> 00:27:48.030
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:27:48.074 --> 00:27:49.682
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:27:49.748 --> 00:27:50.452
Mm-Hmm.

00:27:52.324 --> 00:27:53.204
Excuse me.

00:27:53.730 --> 00:27:54.479
Are you Amanda?

00:27:54.633 --> 00:27:55.470
No, I'm not.

00:27:55.514 --> 00:27:57.341
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:03.265 --> 00:28:05.313
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:06.106 --> 00:28:07.162
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:07.295 --> 00:28:09.342
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:09.783 --> 00:28:11.082
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:12.427 --> 00:28:13.880
There's ways to test that.

00:28:16.082 --> 00:28:17.337
I brought holy water.

00:28:18.218 --> 00:28:19.957
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:20.424 --> 00:28:22.604
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:23.176 --> 00:28:24.123
Oh. Nice.

00:28:26.259 --> 00:28:26.941
Hey.

00:28:27.107 --> 00:28:27.789
What?

00:28:27.965 --> 00:28:28.846
Say it in latin.

00:28:29.132 --> 00:28:29.793
I know.

00:28:29.881 --> 00:28:30.453
Okay.

00:28:30.696 --> 00:28:31.334
Hey!

00:28:31.841 --> 00:28:32.655
What?!

00:28:32.964 --> 00:28:34.791
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:34.901 --> 00:28:36.707
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:28:49.582 --> 00:28:50.705
Hi. Hi.

00:28:51.762 --> 00:28:52.841
Can I help you with something?

00:28:52.929 --> 00:28:53.832
Oh, no.

00:28:53.876 --> 00:28:55.835
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:57.851
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:28:57.961 --> 00:28:59.899
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:29:00.647 --> 00:29:03.686
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:04.820 --> 00:29:06.009
You'd be surprised.

00:29:06.339 --> 00:29:08.276
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:08.959 --> 00:29:10.610
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:11.953 --> 00:29:13.605
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:13.946 --> 00:29:15.025
You're scared to fly?

00:29:16.147 --> 00:29:17.381
Kind of a long story.

00:29:18.514 --> 00:29:20.100
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:20.177 --> 00:29:20.981
It's okay.

00:29:22.335 --> 00:29:23.942
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:25.219 --> 00:29:26.034
No.

00:29:26.562 --> 00:29:28.214
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:28.269 --> 00:29:29.656
I just, uh...

00:29:30.449 --> 00:29:32.408
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:33.685 --> 00:29:34.412
Huh.

00:29:35.436 --> 00:29:36.074
So...

00:29:38.893 --> 00:29:39.685
Cristo.

00:29:40.984 --> 00:29:42.305
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:29:47.547 --> 00:29:48.405
Cristo?

00:29:49.572 --> 00:29:50.783
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:29:51.818 --> 00:29:53.095
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:29:57.296 --> 00:29:58.155
Okay.

00:30:06.100 --> 00:30:08.962
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:09.006 --> 00:30:10.063
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:10.107 --> 00:30:11.439
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:11.461 --> 00:30:13.024
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:13.090 --> 00:30:14.874
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:15.006 --> 00:30:16.063
Anywhere.

00:30:16.856 --> 00:30:19.035
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:19.113 --> 00:30:21.447
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:21.777 --> 00:30:23.340
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:23.385 --> 00:30:24.838
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:24.926 --> 00:30:26.709
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:26.753 --> 00:30:28.063
Yes, you can.

00:30:28.459 --> 00:30:31.388
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:31.432 --> 00:30:32.489
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:32.533 --> 00:30:33.744
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:33.766 --> 00:30:35.836
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:35.946 --> 00:30:36.936
Right now.

00:30:45.901 --> 00:30:46.694
Good.

00:30:47.971 --> 00:30:48.719
Now,

00:30:49.325 --> 00:30:51.659
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:30:52.254 --> 00:30:53.487
The ritual romano.

00:30:54.544 --> 00:30:55.424
What do we have to do?

00:30:55.887 --> 00:30:56.680
It's two parts.

00:30:56.724 --> 00:30:59.146
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:30:59.301 --> 00:31:02.405
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:02.680 --> 00:31:03.451
More powerful?

00:31:03.561 --> 00:31:04.463
Yeah. How?

00:31:05.146 --> 00:31:06.599
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:06.643 --> 00:31:08.471
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:08.735 --> 00:31:10.298
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:10.827 --> 00:31:12.808
Well, because the second part

00:31:13.689 --> 00:31:15.164
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:15.561 --> 00:31:16.728
Once and for all.

00:31:18.247 --> 00:31:19.942
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:31:57.491 --> 00:31:58.423
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:31:58.531 --> 00:31:59.333
Anything?

00:31:59.527 --> 00:32:01.390
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:32:01.650 --> 00:32:02.538
15 minutes.

00:32:03.795 --> 00:32:05.116
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:05.874 --> 00:32:07.390
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:09.613
You believe that?

00:32:10.371 --> 00:32:11.454
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:20.958 --> 00:32:21.933
What? What is it?

00:32:23.255 --> 00:32:23.969
Cristo.

00:32:39.116 --> 00:32:40.286
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:40.437 --> 00:32:41.476
12 minutes, dude.

00:32:43.890 --> 00:32:44.735
Oh, hi.

00:32:45.491 --> 00:32:47.084
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:32:47.157 --> 00:32:49.330
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:32:49.547 --> 00:32:51.430
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:32:51.913 --> 00:32:53.507
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:32:53.871 --> 00:32:56.165
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:32:56.213 --> 00:32:58.362
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:33:00.098 --> 00:33:01.040
Who are you guys?

00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:03.309
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:03.430 --> 00:33:05.820
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:05.893 --> 00:33:06.907
We need your help

00:33:06.979 --> 00:33:08.694
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:08.814 --> 00:33:09.716
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:09.788 --> 00:33:12.638
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:14.110
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:14.255 --> 00:33:15.631
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:15.752 --> 00:33:18.039
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:19.029
He's dead.

00:33:19.712 --> 00:33:20.750
Wait. What?

00:33:20.919 --> 00:33:22.126
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:22.416 --> 00:33:23.961
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:24.106 --> 00:33:25.652
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:25.676 --> 00:33:27.318
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:28.066 --> 00:33:29.853
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:29.878 --> 00:33:31.203
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:31.228 --> 00:33:32.628
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:32.653 --> 00:33:34.303
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:39.609 --> 00:33:40.534
On...

00:33:41.484 --> 00:33:43.209
On 2485,

00:33:43.259 --> 00:33:45.059
There was this man.

00:33:45.109 --> 00:33:47.234
He...had these eyes.

00:33:47.509 --> 00:33:49.162
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:33:49.184 --> 00:33:50.837
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:33:50.859 --> 00:33:52.648
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:33:52.693 --> 00:33:54.754
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:33:54.821 --> 00:33:55.750
Don't have time to explain.

00:33:55.772 --> 00:33:57.199
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:33:57.312 --> 00:33:58.693
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:33:58.738 --> 00:34:00.572
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:34:00.617 --> 00:34:02.293
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:02.338 --> 00:34:03.719
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:03.787 --> 00:34:05.213
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:05.236 --> 00:34:07.410
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:14.008 --> 00:34:14.755
Okay.

00:34:54.834 --> 00:34:55.989
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:02.170 --> 00:35:04.841
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:04.887 --> 00:35:06.358
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:15.397 --> 00:35:16.718
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:16.784 --> 00:35:17.709
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:17.753 --> 00:35:19.537
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:19.581 --> 00:35:21.166
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:21.210 --> 00:35:22.487
Can you do that?

00:35:22.795 --> 00:35:23.380
Amanda?

00:35:23.623 --> 00:35:24.177
Okay.

00:35:24.907 --> 00:35:25.483
Okay.

00:35:27.161 --> 00:35:29.331
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:35:51.248 --> 00:35:52.842
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:35:54.768 --> 00:35:56.318
She must have died screaming!

00:35:57.004 --> 00:35:58.642
Even now, she's burning!

00:36:01.551 --> 00:36:02.260
Sam!

00:36:05.865 --> 00:36:07.038
"Prayer"...

00:36:09.761 --> 00:36:10.470
I got him.

00:36:31.398 --> 00:36:32.018
Where'd he go?

00:36:32.085 --> 00:36:32.992
He's in the plane.

00:36:33.059 --> 00:36:34.564
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:21.895 --> 00:38:22.426
I don't know.

00:38:22.515 --> 00:38:23.733
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:23.976 --> 00:38:25.283
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:25.570 --> 00:38:27.740
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:29.751 --> 00:38:30.902
Anything else?

00:38:31.279 --> 00:38:32.186
No, that's all.

00:38:35.968 --> 00:38:36.920
"Thank you"

00:38:43.318 --> 00:38:44.337
Let's get out of here.

00:38:47.281 --> 00:38:48.123
You okay?

00:38:49.827 --> 00:38:50.580
Dean,

00:38:52.550 --> 00:38:54.166
It knew about Jessica.

00:38:56.841 --> 00:38:59.210
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:38:59.586 --> 00:39:00.317
They lie.

00:39:01.091 --> 00:39:02.309
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:03.992 --> 00:39:04.612
Yeah.

00:39:07.054 --> 00:39:07.829
Come on.

00:39:14.028 --> 00:39:16.370
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:17.787 --> 00:39:19.470
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:20.931 --> 00:39:22.277
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:22.808 --> 00:39:24.137
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:27.369 --> 00:39:28.344
You know, Jerry.

00:39:28.676 --> 00:39:29.251
Yeah.

00:39:29.867 --> 00:39:32.480
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:32.524 --> 00:39:34.162
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:34.428 --> 00:39:35.624
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:36.266 --> 00:39:36.704
What?

00:39:36.749 --> 00:39:38.077
When did you talk to him?

00:39:38.254 --> 00:39:40.690
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:41.110 --> 00:39:43.767
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:39:45.711 --> 00:39:46.508
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:03.400 --> 00:40:04.884
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:04.906 --> 00:40:07.054
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:07.077 --> 00:40:08.383
It's been out of service.

00:40:09.706 --> 00:40:10.902
This is John Winchester.

00:40:11.234 --> 00:40:12.540
I can't be reached.

00:40:12.549 --> 00:40:14.896
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:15.848 --> 00:40:20.648

866-907-3235

00:40:21.644 --> 00:40:22.729
He'll can help.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
